# The openSUSE family's package names for spark-shell (zypper). Tumbleweed,
# and what says ID_LIKE=opensuse (Leap, Slowroll: by family, not proven);
# os-release's own ID there is opensuse-tumbleweed, so the family is the
# ID_LIKE word. A name counts as installed when any installed package
# provides it (rpm -q --whatprovides: python3 is python313's capability).
# Every name was looked up in Tumbleweed's oss repository, and CI looks
# them up again on Tumbleweed itself.
PM=zypper
PKG_SHELL=bash tmux ncurses-utils diffutils starship
PKG_CLI=bat eza fzf zoxide fd jq btop
# curl and ssh-keygen: the dialog, fetched for a release tag whose signature is checked
# swayidle and swaylock: the display off and the lock when idle; grim, slurp and
# wl-clipboard: screen capture, to a file and the clipboard
# brightnessctl and ddcutil: the brightness, a laptop's backlight or a screen's DDC/CI
# rsvg-convert: a drawing drawn again in another palette, a picture's colors read
# (gdk-pixbuf's thumbnailer is gone from Tumbleweed's gdk-pixbuf)
# Mesa-dri: the GPU's own driver for sway, which a minimal install may lack
# no package of Monaspace Neon, the terminal's font, here: spark-shell on fetches the release's zip, its sha256 pinned
# mako: the notifications, and libnotify-tools is notify-send; udisks2: a
# drive plugged in, mounted when asked
PKG_DESKTOP=sway swaybg foot dejavu-fonts Mesa-dri curl openssh-clients swayidle swaylock grim slurp wl-clipboard brightnessctl ddcutil rsvg-convert mako libnotify-tools udisks2
# the sound with the desktop: PipeWire, WirePlumber, its PulseAudio server,
# ALSA programs through it, and the plugins (Bluetooth sound among them)
PKG_SOUND=pipewire wireplumber pipewire-pulseaudio pipewire-alsa pipewire-spa-plugins-0_2
# kbd is setvtrgb and setfont, the console palette and font
PKG_CONSOLE=kbd
# the login screen (spark-shell on login): greetd, swayidle to turn the display
# off when idle, and the account greetd's package makes for it
PKG_LOGIN=greetd swayidle
LOGIN_ACCOUNT=greeter
